    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d559">

                <pb facs="0661" n="593" xml:id="pg593"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/3207</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-02-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 5, 1917</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: The enclosed telegram
                    has just been received from Minister Gonzales, at Habana.<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d559-f1"/> I would like to know your wishes in the reply I am to
                    make to this dispatch. I think we should consider very seriously requesting the
                    Cuban Government to remove the German Consuls and breaking off relations, in
                    view of the proximity of Cuba to this country and to our West Indian
                    possessions.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
